meta {
  name: Clone Site Admin Template
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/radiology-panels/{{siteAdminRadiologyPanelId}}/clone
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "masterDataId": "{{masterDataId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Clone a single SITE_ADMIN radiology-panel template into the caller's tenant.
  Business JWT. **Only `masterDataId` is in the body** — `tenantId` comes from the
  JWT and `branchId` from the target master data (CLAUDE.md §4.7), never the body.

  Deep-copies the template panel with a fresh id, `source = "TENANT"`,
  `clonedFromId = template.id`; the template's referenced SITE_ADMIN tests are
  cloned into the tenant too and the member join rows are rewired — all as TENANT
  records. Returns the new TENANT radiology panel with its tests.

  - `masterDataId` must belong to the caller's tenant → else 404
    `MASTER_DATA_NOT_FOUND`.
  - Name/code conflicts in the target master data → 409
    `RADIOLOGY_PANEL_NAME_CONFLICT` / `RADIOLOGY_PANEL_CODE_CONFLICT`.
  - Set `siteAdminRadiologyPanelId` from "82 SiteAdmin Radiology Panels → Create
    Radiology Panel Template" (its post-response captures it).
}
